WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.620
Hey, welcome to Planetarian Daily, episode 132.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.480
It's July 26th, 2026.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.760
Some interesting findings to cover today.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.500
US researchers mapped how a rare longevity gene

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.920
shields the brain from Alzheimer's pathology.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.520
US scientists trace the mechanism

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.520
by which a rare longevity associated gene variant

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.020
reduces Alzheimer's related brain changes.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.680
The work focuses on how the gene

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.280
alters cellular pathways that normally allow

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.880
toxic protein buildup.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.840
This adds to ongoing efforts tracking which genetic factors

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.500
modify neurodegic duration risk.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.360
The study clarifies one protective route

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:41.660
that may keep circuits functional longer.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.300
A few episodes back, it was cellular aging markers.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.680
This genetic work adds the mechanism

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.900
for how one variant protects circuits.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:53.000
Next up is a finding from field sampling

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.120
in another species.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.640
Researchers identified a cancer in wild catfish

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.660
that appears capable of spreading between individuals.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.880
The finding marks the first documented case

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:05.460
of this type in the species.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:09.280
It expands the known range of transmissible cancers

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.180
beyond the handful previously recorded in mammals

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.240
and molesques.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:17.300
The work comes from field sampling and pathology analysis.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:20.320
No prior examples of contagious tumors

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:23.200
had been confirmed in wild catfish populations.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.360
On a different note, a motor learning study

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.080
tracked brain activity patterns.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:32.180
A study used generative AI to track how mouse brains

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.720
handle new motor learning.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:36.560
Early stages demanded high activity

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:37.980
across multiple regions.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.100
Once the skill stabilized, activity shifted

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.960
to a low energy pattern that maintained performance.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.040
The results illustrate how the nervous system

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.060
reallocates resources after initial acquisition.

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:53.540
The AI model distinguished between the high cost

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:56.300
acquisition phase and the sparse maintenance phase

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.480
in the same animals.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:00.940
Most people assume that once a skill is learned,

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.860
the brain simply keeps working at the same high level

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.580
it needed during the first attempts.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:08.300
In reality, the opposite occurs.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.400
Right now, as you tie your shoes

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.720
or type of familiar sentence, large scale activity

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:15.760
that was required when you first practiced

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.200
has already dropped away.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.880
The generative AI mapping in mice

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:23.020
showed that initial learning recruits widespread regions.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:26.560
Yet mastery collapses that pattern into a sparse,

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:29.380
efficient circuit that still delivers the same output.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:33.040
One memorable illustration is that the energy cost

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.580
of an automated action can fall dramatically

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.180
once the new representation stabilizes.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.900
This matters for anyone building habits.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.100
Repeated practice does not just improve accuracy.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.800
It literally reduces the metabolic load

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.400
the nervous system must carry.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:50.840
Watch for future studies that measure

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:53.580
whether the same efficiency shift appears in humans

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.980
during rehabilitation or language learning.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:59.820
Shifting now to how experienced tuned speech systems.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.740
A Taiwan led study of Mandarin speakers

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:05.240
demonstrated that prior language exposure

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.340
alters both the sounds people produce

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:10.280
and the way they categorize incoming speech.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.600
The team measured acoustic details

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:15.040
and perceptual boundaries across learners

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.300
with different backgrounds.

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:19.320
The findings show that adult speech systems

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:21.720
remain tuned by cumulative experience

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.360
rather than resetting to a universal template.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:27.300
Participants who had learned additional languages

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.560
earlier in life showed distinct shifts

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:31.540
in both production and perception

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.980
compared with monolingual controls.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.180
Now, a study examined behavioral patterns in attention.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:42.100
People with ADHD showed weaker response in a vision

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.640
and greater reliance on automatic habits

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.040
in behavioral tasks.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.180
Brain imaging revealed disrupted coordination

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:52.000
between circuits that support deliberate choices

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.160
and those that encode routines.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.780
The pattern helps explain why stopping

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.960
and ongoing action remains difficult

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.260
even when the person intends to switch.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:04.560
The study compared performance on go, no go

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:07.280
and habit learning paradigms between ADHD

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.720
and control groups.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.620
Moving to registry data on couples,

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.540
a study found spouses of dementia patients

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.980
faced roughly 70% higher likelihood

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.800
of developing the condition themselves.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.980
The data came from large registry records

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.660
tracking couples over time.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:27.080
Shared environment, stress and lifestyle factors

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.800
are under examination as possible contributors.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.660
The elevated incidents persisted

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:34.780
after statistical adjustment for age

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:36.560
and other demographic variables.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.400
On another front, an analysis looked

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.140
at forest management practices.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:45.680
Analysis of more than 18,000 forest patches worldwide

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.880
showed that local customs, not central regulation,

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:52.360
often maintain both crop cycles and forest recovery.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.740
The study examined long-term outcomes

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:57.160
across multiple continents

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:59.640
where slash and burn practices continue.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.960
Results indicate that small-scale societies

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:05.700
can keep soil and canopy conditions stable

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.600
when customary limits on clearing are followed.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.860
Patches managed under strong community norms

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:13.740
regenerated more consistently

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:16.260
than those lacking such informal controls.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.980
Next is a mouse study on circuit responsiveness.

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:22.560
Mild prenatal inflammation in mice

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:24.800
produced lasting brain overactivity,

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:27.260
sensory issues, repetitive behaviors

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.680
and seizure susceptibility in offspring.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:32.640
One dose of rapamycin normalized

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.400
most of these features within about two hours.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.340
The effect was transient, yet it indicates

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:40.740
that adult circuits retain more capacity

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:43.520
for rapid adjustment than earlier models assumed.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.880
The mTOR pathway inhibitor was administered

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:49.020
after the animals had reached adulthood.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:52.600
The rapamycin reversal of autism-like traits

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:56.400
in adult mice shows that certain developmental brain phenotypes

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.920
remain responsive to targeted intervention

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.820
long after the initial insult.

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:04.500
This moves the tracked neuroscience program forward

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:07.220
by demonstrating short-term circuit adaptability

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:09.240
rather than fixed early wiring.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.440
It raises the open question

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:13.900
of whether similar transient windows exist

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:15.720
for other neurodevelopmental

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.620
or neurodegenerative conditions.

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:21.260
The next data to watch are dose ranging studies

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:23.060
and tests in additional models

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:25.860
that clarify how long benefits can be extended.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:28.640
What aspect of adult brain flexibility

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:30.640
would you like to see explored next?

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:33.340
Turning to grassland ecosystems,

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:36.720
ecologists tracked how changes in herbivore species

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:39.320
composition affect predator and plant layers

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:40.860
in grassland systems.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:43.460
Fluctuations at the herbivore level

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.480
propagated through the entire web,

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:47.180
altering stability metrics.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:50.640
The work underscores that multi-layer interactions

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:53.320
rather than single-trophic diversity alone

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:55.140
determine overall resilience.

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:58.340
Data were collected across multiple sites

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:00.840
where herbivore populations varied naturally

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:03.100
or through experimental manipulation.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:07.080
Now, research on exceptional memory in older adults.

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:10.100
Individuals with exceptional late-life memory

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:13.480
showed genetic profiles similar to typical older adults

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:15.860
rather than carrying fewer risk variants.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.540
Researchers conclude that unknown protective processes

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:23.320
in brain, body, or environment likely preserve function.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.580
The finding narrows the search

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:28.580
for non-genetic contributors to cognitive resilience.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:31.760
Super-agers performed at levels comparable

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:34.840
to much younger adults on episodic memory tests

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:36.620
despite their advanced age.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:40.580
Shifting to behavioral patterns around climate actions.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:44.800
A four-year study of nearly 2,800 Australians

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:47.420
found that recycling, dietary shifts,

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:49.480
and similar habits neither boosted

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:51.540
nor lowered later political engagement

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:53.140
on environmental issues.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:56.660
The results counter concerns that individual steps

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.220
crowd out collective action.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:01.600
Participants reported their behaviors and attitudes

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:03.160
at multiple time points,

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:06.920
allowing researchers to test directional effects over time.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:09.560
The study tracked the same individuals

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:12.680
across repeated surveys to separate any influence

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:15.560
of personal habits from broader policy attitudes.

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.500
No measurable shift appeared in willingness

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:20.360
to support systemic reforms

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:21.860
whether participants increased

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:23.820
or maintained their private actions.

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:26.720
The design ruled out reverse causation

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:29.400
by confirming that baseline political engagement

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:32.140
did not predict later changes in daily habits.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:35.600
On the nutrition side, long-term observations

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:37.980
linked coffee intake to liver outcomes.

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:42.220
Long-term data associated even one or two cups daily

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:44.620
with healthier liver imaging and blood markers.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:47.820
Benefits strengthened at three or four cups

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:50.460
and appeared across multiple disease endpoints,

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:53.440
including cirrhosis and liver cancer mortality.

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:55.780
The pattern held after accounting

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:57.420
for other lifestyle variables.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.280
Coffee drinkers also displayed lower levels

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:03.900
of circulating proteins linked to inflammation and fibrosis.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:08.020
Next, a catalog of unusual natural compounds.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:11.320
Researchers cataloged secondary metabolites

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:13.760
containing elements beyond the usual carbon,

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:15.900
hydrogen, nitrogen, oxygen set.

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:18.820
The survey highlights structural diversity

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:21.280
from microbes, plants, and marine sources

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:24.960
that may expand drug discovery and agricultural toolkits.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:28.180
Compounds incorporating halogens, metals,

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:30.700
or other uncommon atoms were identified

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:32.340
across dozens of species.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:36.120
The work draws on published chemical characterizations

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:38.060
rather than new synthesis efforts.

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:40.980
Several of the identified metabolites

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:43.360
showed bioactivity profiles distinct

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:46.380
from those built only from the standard four elements.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:49.380
The catalog includes both terrestrial

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.620
and oceanic examples to illustrate

00:09:51.620 --> 00:09:55.520
how rare atoms appear in natural product libraries worldwide.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:58.740
Moving to a clinical trial on joint pain

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.760
in a six week trial, participants taking

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:05.420
a prebiotic fiber supplement reported reduced knee pain

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:09.100
alongside gains in grip strength and lower pain sensitivity.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.860
The outcomes point to a gut muscle pain axis

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:15.900
that could be targeted with simple dietary additions.

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:19.400
The supplement altered gut microbiota composition,

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.900
which correlated with the observed improvements

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:24.980
in joint symptoms and overall pain thresholds.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:28.680
Grip strength increases occurred alongside the pain reductions

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:31.140
suggesting a broader functional benefit

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:32.640
beyond the target joint.

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:36.760
Pain sensitivity testing used standardized pressure stimuli

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:38.760
applied at multiple body sites

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:41.400
to confirm the change was not limited to the knee.

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:45.000
Microbiota shifts were measured through fecal sampling

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.540
before and after the intervention period.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:51.340
Finally, a physical system that stores multiple states,

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:53.680
a non-brownian suspension was shown

00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:56.780
to hold multiple interacting memory states simultaneously.

00:10:57.640 --> 00:11:00.160
The physical system demonstrates how amplitude

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:02.260
and directional information can coexist

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:04.700
and compete without immediate erasure.

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:07.300
The work provides an analog model

00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:09.340
for studying memory storage dynamics.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:12.140
Experiments tracked how the fluid retained

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:15.460
and retrieved distinct inputs over repeated cycles.

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:18.640
The suspension maintains separate memory traces

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:22.680
even when new inputs overlapped in time with earlier ones.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:26.620
Amplitude encoded information remain distinguishable

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:29.840
from directional information across successive readouts.

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:32.700
Keep an eye on dose ranging follow-ups

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:35.260
from the rapamycin work that may clarify

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:38.480
how long the observed reversibility can be extended.

